==Battleground==
*The enemy base is protected by a [[Base Barrier]] until the boss is defeated.
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 5.33 seconds<sup>160f</sup>, delay 0.67~1 seconds<sup>20f~30f</sup>.
*Infinite [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Croco]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 1.33~1.67 seconds<sup>40f~50f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 46.67~50 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,500f</sup>.
*2 [[Kang Roo]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Pigeon de Sable]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 5.33~8.67 seconds<sup>160f~260f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 1~2 seconds<sup>30f~60f</sup>.
*1 [[Doremi]] spawns as the boss after 36.67 seconds<sup>1,100f</sup>.
*7 [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn after 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
*7 [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn after 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>, delay 0.67~1 seconds<sup>20f~30f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Since the field is filled with weak peons, meatshielding here is not necessary, and may even be detrimental as it might cause Doremi to unleash an attack on your units. Instead, opt for [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave Attackers]] like [[Talents|Talented]] [[Dom Cat (Special Cat)|Dark Lazer]] and [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat]] or spammable [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attackers]] like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]]. Since the peons are spammed at a ridiculous amount, money is not an issue and you can just spam every unit in your lineup without fear of running out of money. If you haven't invested much in Dark Lazer, you can also use research combos with [[Brainwashed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Flying Cat]] instead.

Talented [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] can be used here without consequence unlike [[Baby Fake (Merciless)|Baby Fake]] because he won't run into any backliners, making this stage very easy if owned. Simply lure Doremi to your base, and spawn Awakened Bahamut Cat for an easy win. It is recommended to use [[Cool Japan (Combo)|Cool Japan]] to make this strategy more consistent.

==Trivia==
*Professional Babbler's Japanese name, Babufessional (バブフェッショナル), is derived from the Japanese equivalent of "waah", "boohoo" or "goo-goo ga-ga", ''babū'' (バブー) or ''babubabu'' (バブバブ), and ''professional''.
*In [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]], the first stage to have a [[Base Barrier]] was [[Impending Calamity]], but in other versions, the first was Professional Babbler.

